#: INDISTINGUISHABILITY.md:141
msgid ""
"Chemiscope is invaluable for determining whether our order parameter is good"
" at distinguishing the atoms within the solid from those within the liquid. "
"If you visualize the FCCCUBIC or the transformed values of these parameters "
"in the example above, you see that roughly half of the atoms are solid-like,"
" and nearly half of the atoms are liquid-like. Notice also that we can use "
"the dimensionality reduction that were discussed in earlier parts of this "
"masterclass and clustering algorithms to develop these atomic order "
"parameters. Generating the data to analyze using these algorithms is easier "
"because we can get multiple sets of coordinates to analyze from each "
"trajectory frame. The atoms are, after all, indistinguishable."
msgstr ""

